            <ArticleTitle>Diabetic cardiomyopathy: experimental and clinical observations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>776-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Heart failure, arrhythmia, or chest pain can be a consequence of diabetes independent of coronary disease or hypertension. Diastolic myocardial dysfunction is common, contributing to the high mortality during acute infarction. The authors discuss diabetic cardiomyopathy and its management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
